From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Builder <builder@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm: register osd_reverse as a module parameter

The same defect as 0004 and 0007, reached by a slightly different route,
and the last instance of it in this tree.

meson_logo.c registers four command line handlers. Three of them --
display_bpp=, fb_width= and fb_height= -- call __setup() unguarded, so the
macro still names the handler and the handler still has a reference. The
fourth does not:

    #ifndef MODULE
    __setup("osd_reverse=", drm_logo_reverse_setup);
    #endif

This file is built into aml_drm, which is a module here, so that __setup()
is dropped entirely and drm_logo_reverse_setup() loses its only reference.
Upstream's replacement, ODROID_DRM_LOGO_DEFINE_STRING_PARAM(osd_reverse,
drm_logo_reverse_setup, ...), is the one thing that names it again -- and
it sits behind #ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_MESON_ODROID_COMMON, which this board
config does not set. The result is a static function with no caller and,
because the tree adds -Werror unconditionally for CONFIG_AMLOGIC_DRIVER, a
build that stops:

    meson_logo.c:231:12: error: 'drm_logo_reverse_setup' defined but not
        used [-Werror=unused-function]

Note this is why only one of the four handlers fails. The other three keep
their __setup() reference regardless of MODULE, so they are unaffected and
their ODROID_DRM_LOGO_REGISTER_PARAM entries are carried here only because
they live in the same block, not because they were needed.

As in 0004 and 0007, the fix is to remove the guard and change nothing
else. The block already sits inside #ifndef CONFIG_AMLOGIC_MEDIA_FB, the
same condition that encloses drm_logo_reverse_setup() itself, so after the
guard is dropped the definition and its registration are compiled under
exactly one condition rather than two. CONFIG_AMLOGIC_MEDIA_FB is not set
in this configuration, which is why the function is compiled at all.

With the guard removed the parameters are reachable as aml_drm.osd_reverse=,
aml_drm.display_bpp=, aml_drm.fb_width= and aml_drm.fb_height=. boot.ini
passes none of them and is not changed here.

Runtime effect is NOT VERIFIED. This patch is what makes the file compile.
No board has run this kernel, so whether osd_reverse or the logo geometry
parameters do anything useful on it is unknown and must not be assumed.
---
--- a/common_drivers/drivers/drm/meson_logo.c
+++ b/common_drivers/drivers/drm/meson_logo.c
@@ -268,7 +268,13 @@
 	*reverse_type = osd_info.osd_reverse;
 }
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_ARCH_MESON_ODROID_COMMON
+/*
+ * Module parameter support, un-gated for the same reason as vout_serve.c:
+ * the __setup("osd_reverse=") above sits behind #ifndef MODULE and this
+ * file is built into aml_drm, a module here, so without the registration
+ * below drm_logo_reverse_setup() is a static function with no caller,
+ * which -Werror rejects.
+ */
 static char odroid_osd_reverse_param[32];
 
 static int odroid_drm_logo_get_string(char *buf, const struct kernel_param *kp)
@@ -368,8 +374,6 @@
 
 #endif
 
-#endif
-
 struct para_pair_s {
 	char *name;
 	int value;
